===== written out
class, method, class, method with a parameter -> D
all four with one -> (A1, B, C, D)
each looks in its own -> ('outer', 'inner', 'inner', 'module')
===== what __prepare__() gives
of a metaclass, None -> TypeError: Meta.__prepare__() must return a mapping, not NoneType
   of what is no class -> TypeError: <metaclass>.__prepare__() must return a mapping, not NoneType
of a metaclass, an int -> TypeError: Meta.__prepare__() must return a mapping, not int
   of what is no class -> TypeError: <metaclass>.__prepare__() must return a mapping, not int
of a metaclass, a list -> TypeError: list indices must be integers or slices, not str
   of what is no class -> TypeError: list indices must be integers or slices, not str
of a metaclass, a str -> TypeError: string indices must be integers, not 'str'
   of what is no class -> TypeError: string indices must be integers, not 'str'
of a metaclass, a tuple -> TypeError: tuple indices must be integers or slices, not str
   of what is no class -> TypeError: tuple indices must be integers or slices, not str
of a metaclass, a set -> TypeError: Meta.__prepare__() must return a mapping, not set
   of what is no class -> TypeError: <metaclass>.__prepare__() must return a mapping, not set
of a metaclass, an object -> TypeError: Meta.__prepare__() must return a mapping, not object
   of what is no class -> TypeError: <metaclass>.__prepare__() must return a mapping, not object
of a metaclass, what can be subscripted -> ZeroDivisionError: division by zero
   of what is no class -> ZeroDivisionError: division by zero
of a metaclass, a dict -> X
   of what is no class -> made
of a metaclass, a mapping of its own -> X
   of what is no class -> made
===== a dict that is given to an instance
plain -> ([1, 2], ['a', 'b'], 2, True)
keys of a class derived from str -> ([1, 2], ['a', 'b'], 2, True)
that has its own idea of what it is equal to -> (['none', 2], ['a', 'b'], 2, True)
other keys -> (['none', 2], ['1', 'None', 'b'], 3, True)
set afterwards -> (None, 1, None, 2, None, 3, True, True, 2, 3, False)
done
